{
  "_comment": [
    "run_revit_code policy (spec 7.8). DENY BY DEFAULT: a System type is usable only when it is listed in system_types, a RevitAPIUI type only when it is listed in revit_ui_types, and a RevitAPI type unless a rule below denies it.",
    "This file is the source of truth. It is compiled into the signed add-in as BinaVibe/Copilot/Code/CodePolicyTable.cs; CodePolicyTests.Table_MatchesJson fails when the two differ. The cloud cannot configure any of it.",
    "Rules are checked in order; the first rule that matches names the category. Every category has a golden test in Tests/CodePolicyTests.cs (CodePolicyTests.EveryCategoryHasAGoldenCase): change the policy only together with its test.",
    "Rule kinds: syntax and operation are structural checks done by the engine (match lists the construct names it knows); system_namespace / system_type / system_member label denied System symbols; system_default denies every System type not in system_types; revit_type / revit_namespace deny Revit types; revit_member denies Revit members whose name matches a regex; revit_setter denies assigning a Revit property; path_parameter denies Revit members taking a path; revit_ui_default denies every RevitAPIUI type not in revit_ui_types; assembly_default denies anything from any other assembly.",
    "mode decides read versus write (ModeClassifier): any document-modifying symbol makes the call a write, which is previewed and needs the drafter's approval."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "language_version": "CSharp10",
